# Mentorma APK Build Notes

## Prerequisites

Install Node.js 18+ and the Expo CLI toolchain on a machine that has Android SDK support.

```bash
npm install -g eas-cli
npm install -g expo-cli
```

Then in this project:

```bash
npm install
npx expo install
```

## Local Android build

```bash
npx expo run:android
```

This generates an Android app and is the usual step before building an APK.

## APK build through Expo EAS

```bash
npx eas-cli build -p android --profile preview
```

This produces a build artifact suitable for APK installation or internal distribution.

## Production release

```bash
npx eas-cli build -p android --profile production
```

## Notes

This repository includes the app shell and product MVP assets, but the actual APK file must be generated from a local machine or CI environment with Android SDK / Gradle / EAS build access enabled.

This environment can prepare the project, but cannot directly install Android toolchains or access the device SDK needed to finalize the signed APK binary.
